WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:01.660
Speaker 1: Welcome back to The David Pakman
Show.

00:00:01.660 --> 00:00:04.190
I'm producer Pat Forde, filling in for David
today.

00:00:04.190 --> 00:00:08.560
He is on vacation and will be back at the
end of the week in response to the mass shooting

00:00:08.560 --> 00:00:11.809
that took place in Tennessee a couple of weeks
back.

00:00:11.809 --> 00:00:17.040
Republicans who are in control of the state
legislature have decided to take action, but

00:00:17.040 --> 00:00:21.670
not in any sort of substantive way, not by
strengthening background checks or banning

00:00:21.670 --> 00:00:23.740
certain types of weapons.

00:00:23.740 --> 00:00:28.550
Instead, they've decided to expel two members
of the legislative body who took part in the

00:00:28.550 --> 00:00:34.840
protest and essentially broke the rules of
decorum in the legislative body in so doing.

00:00:34.840 --> 00:00:39.559
Tennessee lawmakers expelled two members from
the state legislature just to Jones and Justin

00:00:39.559 --> 00:00:44.090
Peterson after they and a third member, Gloria
Johnson, took part in a protest against gun

00:00:44.090 --> 00:00:46.399
violence from the floor of the chamber.

00:00:46.399 --> 00:00:52.050
The vote took place last Thursday with Johnson
surviving expulsion by only a single vote.

00:00:52.050 --> 00:00:57.120
Notably, Jones and Pierson are black, whereas
Johnson, the one who survived the expulsion

00:00:57.120 --> 00:00:58.120
vote, is white.

00:00:58.120 --> 00:01:02.239
I'll leave it up to you to decide whether
that has anything to do with the results.

00:01:02.239 --> 00:01:07.600
Following the mass shooting, there was a protest
at the legislative chamber to try to get lawmakers

00:01:07.600 --> 00:01:13.020
to do anything at all about this issue of
gun violence and using their position as representatives

00:01:13.020 --> 00:01:15.750
to be actually inside the House chamber.

00:01:15.750 --> 00:01:20.450
These three lawmakers used a bullhorn and
temporarily disrupted the official business

00:01:20.450 --> 00:01:25.550
of the legislative body, leading the Republican
supermajority to call for a recess.

00:01:25.550 --> 00:01:28.860
Let's take a look at some of the video of
the protests taking place.

00:01:28.860 --> 00:01:29.860
We have heard.

00:01:29.860 --> 00:01:35.390
Speaker 3: A lot about.

00:01:35.390 --> 00:01:44.710
Unidentified: Thank you.

00:01:44.710 --> 00:01:48.159
You are being heard.

00:01:48.159 --> 00:01:52.700
Speaker 1: Now, after this happened, Republicans
who hold a large majority of seats immediately

00:01:52.700 --> 00:01:54.500
pledged a rapid response.

00:01:54.500 --> 00:01:56.810
They stripped Johnson and Jones of committee
assignments.

00:01:56.810 --> 00:02:00.680
I don't believe Pierson yet had any committee
assignments.

00:02:00.680 --> 00:02:05.799
Motions to expel the three from the legislature
were introduced by three different members

00:02:05.799 --> 00:02:11.129
of the state legislature on April 3rd, accusing
the trio of disorderly behavior.

00:02:11.129 --> 00:02:16.620
Now, to put this in context, it's very rare
for expulsions to take place in the Tennessee

00:02:16.620 --> 00:02:18.040
legislature.

00:02:18.040 --> 00:02:22.500
Just eight lawmakers have been expelled from
the House in the state's history.

00:02:22.500 --> 00:02:27.480
Six of those were confederates who were expelled
in the 19th century for refusing to affirm

00:02:27.480 --> 00:02:31.010
the citizenship of formerly enslaved black
people.

00:02:31.010 --> 00:02:36.700
In the 20th century, a legislator was expelled
after being convicted of bribery, and most

00:02:36.700 --> 00:02:40.810
recently in 2016, a member was expelled for
sexual misconduct.

00:02:40.810 --> 00:02:44.780
So this expulsion wasn't really about the
merits.

00:02:44.780 --> 00:02:48.849
It only happened because Republicans had the
votes to be able to do it, and they took advantage

00:02:48.849 --> 00:02:49.849
of that.

00:02:49.849 --> 00:02:54.120
And in fact, Justin Jones, one of the two
ousted members, highlighted in a speech that

00:02:54.120 --> 00:02:58.180
he gave on the floor, some of the things that
his fellow members of the legislature did

00:02:58.180 --> 00:03:03.480
over the years, or at least were accused of
doing that, did ultimately not result in an

00:03:03.480 --> 00:03:04.480
expulsion.

00:03:04.480 --> 00:03:05.860
Let's take a look at him talking about that.

00:03:05.860 --> 00:03:08.340
Speaker 4: Let's talk about expulsion.

00:03:08.340 --> 00:03:16.030
For years, One of your colleagues who was
admitted child molester sat in this chamber.

00:03:16.030 --> 00:03:18.450
No expulsion.

00:03:18.450 --> 00:03:23.240
One member sits in this chamber who was found
guilty of domestic violence.

00:03:23.240 --> 00:03:30.939
No expulsion.

00:03:30.939 --> 00:03:36.530
We had a former speaker sits in this chamber
who is now under federal investigation.

00:03:36.530 --> 00:03:37.530
No expulsion.

00:03:37.530 --> 00:03:40.830
We have a member still under federal investigation.

00:03:40.830 --> 00:03:43.290
No expulsion.

00:03:43.290 --> 00:03:52.500
We had a member P in another member's chair
in this chamber.

00:03:52.500 --> 00:03:54.390
No expulsion.

00:03:54.390 --> 00:03:57.040
In fact, they're in leadership now.

00:03:57.040 --> 00:04:02.230
Speaker 1: The hope is that from a political
standpoint, this will backfire on Republicans,

00:04:02.230 --> 00:04:06.480
because not only has this brought the issue
of gun violence more to the forefront and

00:04:06.480 --> 00:04:12.250
how members of Congress at the state and federal
level aren't really doing anything about it.

00:04:12.250 --> 00:04:16.390
It's also made these three national figures,
the Tennessee three, as they're now being

00:04:16.390 --> 00:04:17.390
called.

00:04:17.390 --> 00:04:21.570
Vice President Kamala Harris visited the lawmakers
in Nashville on Friday, and President Biden

00:04:21.570 --> 00:04:26.390
also spoke with the three via conference call
inviting them to visit the White House.

00:04:26.390 --> 00:04:31.449
Now, to be clear, I don't know if disrupting
proceedings and using a bullhorn is the right

00:04:31.449 --> 00:04:36.100
way to go about protesting this sort of matter,
despite it being peaceful, of course, and

00:04:36.100 --> 00:04:41.060
despite it being clearly intended to only
being to be a temporary disruption.

00:04:41.060 --> 00:04:44.970
And that's because if, let's say the shoe
was on the other foot, let's say, you know,

00:04:44.970 --> 00:04:50.320
at the Capitol, we saw Marjorie Taylor GREENE
and Lauren Boebert do this exact same thing

00:04:50.320 --> 00:04:52.980
on one of the issues that they care about.

00:04:52.980 --> 00:04:54.910
Would we be totally fine with it?

00:04:54.910 --> 00:04:56.280
I'm not sure.

00:04:56.280 --> 00:04:58.000
I just want to stay consistent on this.

00:04:58.000 --> 00:04:59.000
Right.

00:04:59.000 --> 00:05:03.120
Nevertheless, I think that expulsion would
be way too extreme if that was to take place.

00:05:03.120 --> 00:05:07.600
I think the most appropriate thing to do in
that sort of instance would be maybe a censure.

00:05:07.600 --> 00:05:08.600
Right.

00:05:08.600 --> 00:05:11.750
Because these people were duly elected to
represent their constituents.

00:05:11.750 --> 00:05:15.720
And barring some sort of extreme event, they
should be able to serve out their term.

00:05:15.720 --> 00:05:19.650
So I think censuring them, which is basically
just an official condemnation, would have

00:05:19.650 --> 00:05:24.380
made a lot more sense for something like this,
breaking the rules of decorum.

00:05:24.380 --> 00:05:28.979
But Republicans in this situation, they were
just trying to abuse their power and be vindictive

00:05:28.979 --> 00:05:30.169
on this matter.

00:05:30.169 --> 00:05:31.850
And then final point I want to make on this.

00:05:31.850 --> 00:05:36.320
Some on the right are comparing this to January
6th, when there's absolutely no comparison

00:05:36.320 --> 00:05:39.569
to be drawn here to the Capitol insurrection.

00:05:39.569 --> 00:05:44.000
On that day, January six, 2021, we saw rioters
beating up cops.

00:05:44.000 --> 00:05:46.170
We saw the Senate chamber get overtaken.

00:05:46.170 --> 00:05:48.320
We saw several people die.

00:05:48.320 --> 00:05:52.690
Based on, you know, because of what happened,
it was directed and then not put a stop to

00:05:52.690 --> 00:05:54.660
by the then president of the United States.

00:05:54.660 --> 00:05:58.600
And the intent of the protests that became
a riot was to overthrow the government, to

00:05:58.600 --> 00:06:00.380
end democracy in the United States.

00:06:00.380 --> 00:06:06.199
This, on the other hand, was a peaceful protest
That was yeah, sure, at times a little rowdy.

00:06:06.199 --> 00:06:08.690
But there was no intention of overthrowing
the government.

00:06:08.690 --> 00:06:11.270
There was no clear acts of violence.

00:06:11.270 --> 00:06:15.139
And it was not intended to end democracy in
the state of Tennessee.

00:06:15.139 --> 00:06:17.000
So spare me those comparisons.

00:06:17.000 --> 00:06:19.210
It will be interesting to see what happens
next.

00:06:19.210 --> 00:06:22.660
And Pierson and Jones, the two who were expelled
from the legislature, will be able to run

00:06:22.660 --> 00:06:23.950
for their seats again.

00:06:23.950 --> 00:07:34.690
Let's hope that they're able to win back their
seats and then all will be good.

